b=Book('04','Pricing, Billing & Economics','Pricing-Billing-Economics','Exact catalog prices, entitlements and balances, financial state transitions, and cost assumptions.');b.intro()
b.section('What the prices mean','''The owner asked this series to use the current codebase pricing. The canonical commercial catalog is src/lib/billing/catalog.ts. Its USD subscription, action, pack and offer values are reproduced here. These are implemented catalog definitions, not proof that every price is synchronized to Stripe, that every promotion is currently active, or that production has no account-specific override.

Mellox has several different units. General credits buy AI/content actions; Video Credits buy video; Pro and Flash messages have their own allowance counters; social publishing has fair-use counts rather than general-credit charges. A separate link-placement purchase subsystem also uses credit terminology and payment code. Do not mix those ledgers.

One general credit has a one-cent catalog face value. It is not a guaranteed one-cent provider cost or cash-equivalent balance. One Video Credit is stored as 100 integer video units, allowing quarter or half units without floating-point money. The current owner billing account shares balances across that owner's brands. Workspace roles still constrain spending.''',('src/lib/billing/catalog.ts','src/server/billing/accounts.server.ts','src/server/billing/meters.server.ts','src/server/links/credits.server.ts'))
