b.section('Video credits, native quotes and output lengths','''A Video Credit is not a general credit. Current video options use integer videoUnits and product feature gates. The tables below reproduce catalog reference options; the provider model registry separately determines valid native resolution/duration and references. For example premium's catalog label is not permission to request a resolution unsupported by the selected upstream provider.

videoUnitsFor prices a UGC request from its option, seconds, resolution band and estimated provider cost. The result is at least the catalog match or a cost-based floor. It rounds to quarter-VC steps, with a minimum of 0.25 VC. USD_PER_VC_REFERENCE is $0.844, and MAX_USD_PER_VC is $1.01. These are code guard parameters, not an advertised sale price or measured average cost.

For an exact option, the cost floor in integer units is max(1, ceil(cost / 1.01 x 4)) x 25. For an unmatched option, the proportional quote uses max(1, ceil(cost / .844 x 4)) x 25 and still respects the floor. The routed provider's actual capabilities and reference-image costs matter.

Studio's default ten-second video uses an explicit two-VC quote and scales by ten-second blocks: ceil(seconds / 10) x 200 units. A sixty-second Studio output therefore quotes 12 VC. It may require multiple provider clips and FFmpeg assembly; it is not equivalent to a single eight-second Standard UGC option.''',('src/lib/billing/catalog.ts','src/lib/ugc/duration.ts','src/server/ugc/models.server.ts','src/server/billing/ugc-async.server.ts','src/server/billing/studio-async.server.ts'))
