b.section('Financial lifecycle and idempotency','''A paid action resolves the acting user's role, owner billing account, current plan/add-ons/overrides and effective enforcement mode. Viewer restrictions remain even in billing maintenance or shadow mode. It checks frozen brands and feature eligibility before acquiring a hold. The hold is keyed by the caller, action and idempotency key.

Success captures all or the supported partial amount; definitive failure releases unused balance. Async Studio and UGC jobs preserve the hold across polls and reconcile it from final job status. A retry of an accepted or finished charge does not create a second independent hold. A dropped HTTP response must not become a free path or a double charge.

The enforcement modes are off, shadow and on. Current global default is on in production and off outside production when no explicit BILLING_ENFORCEMENT is supplied. Shadow records decisions without applying ordinary charging. Production must not silently become unlimited because the schema or an entitlement query is missing; readiness has an explicit unavailable response when required.

Account subscription purchase processing uses Stripe price mappings and signed webhook handling. A return to the success page alone is not proof of payment. Grants, subscription windows, refunds/clawbacks and manual activations need durable, replay-safe records. There is separate Stripe code for link purchase packs; its customer/credit mapping is not the owner-account subscription system.''',('src/server/billing/mode.server.ts','src/server/billing/metered.server.ts','src/server/billing/meters.server.ts','src/server/billing/async-charges.server.ts','src/server/billing/stripe-account.server.ts','src/server/billing/stripe.server.ts','src/app/api/public/hooks/stripe/route.ts'))
b.diagram('Request + verified role + owner account','Resolve plan / availability / restrictions','Hold balance with stable replay key','Execute or advance durable job','Capture success / partial success OR release failure','Webhook / worker reconciliation -> append-only financial evidence')
