b.section('Unit economics without invented production numbers','''No current invoices or measured usage distributions were supplied, so a defensible actual gross margin, fixed monthly operating total or break-even forecast cannot be calculated. Older workbook forecasts are historical assumptions and are not carried forward as current business facts.

The scenario below illustrates arithmetic from current allowances. It assumes every included general credit is consumed at $0.002 provider cost, every VC costs $0.844, each Pro message costs $0.048 and each Flash message $0.009. Those are planning assumptions, not observed average costs. The scenario excludes included research/scans, publishing, infrastructure, payment fees, support, refunds, taxes and free users. It is therefore a variable-AI-cost sensitivity view, not business gross margin.

General-credit usage cannot be valued at face value to compute cash revenue: credits already included in a subscription create no extra cash when spent. Likewise unused allowances, paid packs and promotional restricted grants have different economics. Use actual allocated subscription revenue and task-level accepted-result cost for a measured contribution report.''')
rows=[]
for p in plans[1:]:
    a=p['allowances'];c=a['credits']*.002+a['videoUnits']/100*.844+a['proMessages']*.048+a['flashMessages']*.009
    rows.append([p['label'],f"${c:.2f}",f"{100*(1-c/p['priceMonthlyUsd']):.1f}%",f"{100*(1-c/(p['priceAnnualUsd']/12)):.1f}%"])
b.table(['Plan','Illustrative AI cost','Monthly remainder %','Annual-month remainder %'],rows,[1,1,1.3,1.6])
b.h('Measured operating model to maintain')
b.bullets('Capture by task: provider/model, input/output/reasoning/cache usage, reported USD cost, search/extract calls, render seconds, retry count, outcome and accepted result.','Reconcile monthly: Railway compute/network, Supabase DB/auth/backups, R2 capacity/operations, Redis, AI invoices, social provider tier, research providers, email, monitoring and Stripe fees.','Allocate account-level included work across brands, and record free/promotional consumption separately from paid recurring customers.','Compute contribution = recognized revenue - attributable variable costs; compute operating result only after fixed costs.','Re-price the expensive tail: long video, large crawls, deep Pro/agent runs and repeated failed renders. Do not derive these from one average token price.')
